# Netlify redirect rules.
#
# One job: send the .netlify.app hostname to the custom domain.
#
# Netlify did not do this on its own. On 2026-08-15 all of these answered HTTP 200
# with the same ETag — byte-identical documents at four addresses:
#
#   https://star-stuff.netlify.app/design
#   https://star-stuff.netlify.app/design.html
#   https://starstuff.earth/design
#   https://starstuff.earth/design.html
#
# 110 pages × 4 = 440 crawlable URLs for 110 documents, and search engines split a
# page's ranking signals across duplicates rather than picking a winner. In the 30
# days to 2026-08-15, google.com sent 35 referrals against 15,049 pageviews — near
# zero for a site with a maintained sitemap, real headings and JSON-LD throughout.
# The duplication is the most likely reason the technical SEO is returning nothing.
#
# It also fixes an inbound link. stimpunks.org's /star-stuff/ hub — in their main
# nav under Learn, and our single best referrer — links star-stuff.netlify.app, not
# starstuff.earth. Those readers now land on the canonical host. Better still, get
# the links themselves updated; this is the safety net, not the fix.
#
# The `!` is required. Without it a redirect only fires when no file exists at the
# path, and a file exists at every one of these paths, so every rule would be dead.
#
# WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: canonicalize /design.html -> /design (or the
# reverse) on starstuff.earth. Netlify serves both forms itself and its Pretty URLs
# post-processing can redirect between them; a rule pointing the other way would
# make an infinite loop and take the whole site down. The house convention already
# settles this the safe way — sitemap.xml, every internal link and every
# <link rel="canonical"> say `.html`, which is the standard mechanism for exactly
# this and needs no redirect. Leave it alone.
#
# This consolidates the URL surface. It will not make the pageview count smaller —
# a crawler hitting the old host now gets a 301 and follows it, which is still two
# log entries. The point is that Google finally sees one page instead of four.

https://star-stuff.netlify.app/*  https://starstuff.earth/:splat  301!
http://star-stuff.netlify.app/*   https://starstuff.earth/:splat  301!
